pping_fee(Decimal("50.00"), "RO") returns 4.99 instead of 0.00 and shipping_fee(Decimal("-1.00"), "RO") returns 4.99 instead of raising ValueError. Both required behaviours of the committed requirement are absent.","evidence":[{"kind":"file","ref":"src/pricing/shipping.py","quote":"def shipping_fee(subtotal: Decimal, country: str) -> Decimal:
    fee_by_country = {"RO": Decimal("4.99"), "DE": Decimal("9.99")}
    try:
        fee = fee_by_country[country]"},{"kind":"file","ref":"specs/shipping/spec.md","quote":"an order to `RO` or `DE` whose subtotal is 50.00 or more ships free (fee 0.00)"}],"suggested_fix":"WHEN the subtotal is 50.00 or more for RO/DE or negative for any country THEN the committed code ignores it and returns the flat country fee (or raises UnsupportedShippingCountry for other countries) instead of 0.00 or ValueError."},{"severity":"minor","criterion":null,"title":"Implementer hint undercounts the gate results","detail":"The hint claims "Gate passed: 17 tests and Ruff" while the gate report lists more tests overall (including e2e); harmless but inaccurate.","evidence":[{"kind":"log","ref":"gate report","quote":"setup: pass / lint: pass / test: pass / e2e: pass"}],"suggested_fix":"WHEN summarizing gate results THEN the implementer counts only the tests actually listed in the report."}],"riskiest_assumptions":["The gate report accurately reflects the committed head, so the two tests in tests/test_shipping.py were actually executed and passed against this exact shipping.py.","No other committed file (e.g. a wrapper in pricing/__init__.py or a cart integration) adds the subtotal-based free-shipping or negative-subtotal logic that shipping.py itself lacks.","The two listed criteria are the only ones I must score, so the unimplemented free-shipping and ValueError clauses count as findings rather than additional failing criteria."]}
